OL,3,GNEWSASecond Scottish independence
OL,4,Areferendum 'a long way off' - Offord
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe leader of Reform UK in Scotland has
OL,7,Fsaid a second independence referendum
OL,8,Fis "a long way off".
OL,10,FThe Scottish government last week
OL,11,Fpublished its draft independence
OL,12,Freferendum bill, setting out the
OL,13,Fdetails of the proposed question and
OL,14,Fwho would be allowed to vote.
OL,16,FBut Malcolm Offord told BBC Radio
OL,17,FScotland's Mornings programme that
OL,18,Fthere would need to be a "groundswell"
OL,19,Fof support for a fresh poll.
OL,21,FIn 2014 Scotland voted against becoming
OL,22,Fan independent country by 55% to 45%.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
